{
    "background_story": "Capri was a quiet, unassuming artist who lived in a small studio apartment in the city. She spent most of her days creating intricate paintings that few people ever saw. Despite her talent, Capri never sought to draw attention to herself or her work. She believed that her art was insignificant in the grand scheme of things and that she was just a small, irrelevant speck in the universe. As a result, she never bothered to showcase her work or seek recognition. Her friends and family would often try to convince her to share her art with the world, but Capri was content with the obscurity. She found solace in the unimportance of her existence, free from the pressures of expectation and criticism. In her own small way, Capri was happy, and that was all that mattered to her.",
